Maybe... :)
 
Actually, I wasn't thinking of higher dimensions as the problem.
Even in one, two or three dimensions, I'm not sure what to put
in the x1 of cimde. Etymologically, "dimension" must mean something
like "measurement", but I don't think that helps much. If we take
it literally, then any object can have an infinite number of them.
 
It makes sense to say that an object is two-dimensional.
It makes almost no sense to say that there are exactly two things
that are the dimensions of an object.
 
